speechtext:
Mr. W. D. EULER (North Waterloo) presented the third report of the select standing committee on Railways and Shipping, owned, operated and controlled by the government as follows:
The attention of your committee having been drawn to the omission from the interim supply voted by parliament during the present session, of any part of items 372 and 373, of the estimates 1926-27 respecting loans to the Canadian National Railway and the Canadian Government Merchant Marine, Limited;
Your committee therefore recommends that parliament grant as interim supply the sum of $10,000,000 of the said item 372 and the sum of $200,000 of the said item 373.
